    "chunk_size_bytes": 1995,
    "chunk_text": "2AI fldgi: (I) fPoh \u2013 Y%S ,xld m%cd;dka;%sl iudcjd\u00a7 ckrcfha w;s \u00fafYI .ei\u00dc m;%h \u2013 2019'08'05PART I: SEC. (I) \u2013 GAZETTE EXTRAORDINARY OF THE DEMOCRATIC SOCIALIST REPUBLIC OF SRI LANKA \u2013 05.08.2019\n\nMy No.: IR/COM/03/2017/238.\n\nMr. P. K. Ajantha, No. 118 N/19, Egodakanatta, Bope, Galle.of the one part\n\nand\n\nSouthern Provincial Road Development Authority, No. 19, Lower Dickson Road, Galle.of the other part\n\nSTATEMENT OF MATTER IN DISPUTE\n\nThe matter in dispute between the aforesaid parties is\n\nWhether the suspension and / or the deferment of the salary increment due to Mr. P. K. Ajantha as at 02.04.2015 by theemployer, the Southern Provincial Road Development Authority is just and if not so, to what relief he is entitled.\n\nA. WIMALAWEERA,Commissioner General of Labour.\n\nDated at the office of the Commissioner General of Labour,Colombo, this 01st day of July, 2019.\n\n08 \u2013 734\n\nMy No.: IR/COM/02/2018/102.\n\nTHE INDUSTRIAL DISPUTES ACT, CHAPTER 131 OF THE LEGISLATIVE ENACTMENTS OF CEYLON( 1956 REVISED EDITION)\n\nOrder under Section 4 (1)\n\nWHEREAS an industrial dispute in respect of the matter specified in the statement of the Commissioner of Labour whichaccompanies this order exists between,\n\n1. Mr. R. M. Thanuja Kumara Ranaraja, No. 600, Meepitiya, Kegalle.2. Mr. M. P. P. Wijewardana, Kuruduwatta, Niripola, Hanwella. of the one part\n\nand\n\nDiana Trading Company (Private) Limited, Weragama, Kaykawala, Matale.of the other part\n\nNOW THEREFORE I, Ravindra Samaraweera, Minister of Labour and Trade Union Relations do by virtue of the powersvested in me by Section 4(1) of the Industrial Disputes Act, Chapter 131 of the Legislative Enactments of Ceylon (1956 RevisedEdition), as amended by Acts, Nos. 14 of 1957, 4 of 1962 and 39 of 1968 (read with Industrial Disputes-Special Provisions) Act,No. 37 of 1968 hereby appoint Miss. H. M. Anulawathi, No. 599, Gohagoda Road, Katugastota to be the arbitrator and refer theaforesaid dispute to her for settlement by arbitration."
  },
