    "chunk_text": "NOW THEREFORE I, Ravindra Samaraweera, Minister of Labour and Trade Union Relations do by virtue of the powersvested in me by Section 4(1) of the Industrial Disputes Act, Chapter 131 of the Legislative Enactments of Ceylon (1956 RevisedEdition), as amended by Acts, Nos. 14 of 1957, 4 of 1962 and 39 of 1968 (read with Industrial Disputes-Special Provisions) Act,No. 37 of 1968 hereby appoint Miss. H. M. Anulawathi, No. 599, Gohagoda Road, Katugastota to be the arbitrator and refer theaforesaid dispute to her for settlement by arbitration.\n\nColombo,24th July, 2019.\n\nI fldgi: (I) fPoh \u2013 Y%S ,xld m%cd;dka;%sl iudcjd\u00a7 ckrcfha w;s \u00fafYI .ei\u00dc m;%h \u2013 2019'08'05PART I: SEC. (I) \u2013 GAZETTE EXTRAORDINARY OF THE DEMOCRATIC SOCIALIST REPUBLIC OF SRI LANKA \u2013 05.08.20193A\n\nMy No.: IR/COM/02/2018/102.\n\nTHE INDUSTRIAL DISPUTES ACT, CHAPTER 131 OF THE LEGISLATIVE ENACTMENTS OF CEYLON( 1956 REVISED EDITION)\n\n1. Mr. R. M. Thanuja Kumara Ranaraja, No. 600, Meepitiya, Kegalle.2. Mr. M. P. P. Wijewardana, Kuruduwatta, Niripola, Hanwella. of the one part\n\nand\n\nDiana Trading Company (Private) Limited, Weragama, Kaykawala, Matale.of the other part\n\nSTATEMENT OF MATTER IN DISPUTE\n\nThe matter in dispute between the aforesaid parties is\n\nWhether Mr. R. M. Thanuja Kumara Ranaraja and Mr. P. P. Wijewardana employed in the Diana Trading Company (Private)Limited are entitled for,\n\n1. The monthly fixed allowance2. Vehicle allowance and3. Field allowance.And whether they had been caused injustice by the non-payment of those allowances and if so, to what relief they are entitled.\n\nA. WIMALAWEERA,Commissioner General of Labour.\n\nDated at the office of the Commissioner General of Labour,Colombo, this 08th day of July, 2019.\n\n08 \u2013 735\n\nMy No.: IR/COM/04/2018/144.\n\nTHE INDUSTRIAL DISPUTES ACT CHAPTER 131 OF THE LEGISLATIVE ENACTMENTS OF CEYLON( 1956 REVISED EDITION)\n\nOrder under Section 4 (1)"
