    "chunk_text": "1AIII fldgi \u2013 Y%S ,xld m%cd;dka;%sl iudcjd\u00a7 ckrcfha w;s \u00fafYI .ei\u00dc m;%h \u2013 2019'08'13PART III \u2013 GAZETTE EXTRAORDINARY OF THE DEMOCRATIC SOCIALIST REPUBLIC OF SRI LANKA \u2013 13.08.2019\n\nTHE LAND ACQUISITION ACT (CHAPTER 460)\n\nORDER UNDER SECTION 39A(1)\n\nTHE allotment specified in the Order No. 215 of 2016 made underthe Proviso (a) to Section 38 of the Land Acquisition Act(Chapter 460) and published in the Gazette Extra OrdinaryNo. 1983/34 dated 09.09.2016 is vested absolutely in the State andthe possession of which has been taken for or on behalf of the Stateunder Para (a) of Section 40 of the aforesaid Act. But by the virtue ofpowers vested in me by sub-section (1) of Section 39(a) (inserted byAct, No. 8 of 1979) of the Land Acquisition Act. I, GayanthaKarunatilleke, Minister of Lands and Parliamentary Reforms,do hereby divest only the alltoment described in the Schedule below.\n\nGayantha Karunatilleke,Minister of Lands and Parliamentary Reforms.\n\nMy Ref. No.: 4-3/7/2016/HW/119.Divisional Secretary\u2019s No.: 3/3/22-1.Ministry of Lands and Parliamentary Reforms,\u201cMihikatha Medura\u201d,Rajamalwatta Avenue,Battaramulla.11th July, 2019.\n\nSCHEDULE\n\nAn Allotment of land depicted in the Preliminary Plan No.F.V.P. 1491 prepared by the Surveyor-General, situated in the Villagecalled Bambaragahapelessa in the Grama Niladhari Division No. 854of Godawita in the Minor Division of Rekopattu Korale in theDivisional Secretary\u2019s Division of Weerambugedara in KurunegalaDistrict of Northwestern Province and bounded as follows:\n\n01. Lot No. 151 \u2013 Hitinawatta, Paluwatta aliasMeegahamulawatta \u2013 Extent: About 0.0333 HectareNorth: Lot Nos. 158 and 145; East: Lot Nos. 150 and 19; South:Lot Nos. 19, 34 and 152; West: Lot Nos. 152, 157 and 158.\n\n08 \u2013 962\n\nY%S ,xld m%cd;dka;%sl iudcjd\u00a7 ckrcfha .ei\u00dc m;%hThe Gazette of the Democratic Socialist Republic of Sri Lanka\n\nw;s \u00fafYI EXTRAORDINARY\n\n(Published by Authority)\n\nPART III \u2013 LANDS\n\nLand Redemption Notices"
