    "chunk_size_bytes": 1908,
    "chunk_text": "2.The camp are for abode of pilgrims shall be the land demarcated by the 37th Mile post of Mahiyangana-Bibilamain road up to the 1/39 culvert in front of Mahiyangana National School,and the land situated between theMahiyangana-Meegahakiula road the leading to the clock tower in front of Mahiyangana hospital and new highway.\n\n3.No person shall cook meals in \u201cVihara Maluwa\u2019,'Dewala Boomiya\u201d, \u201cPalle Veediya\u201d (The court yards of the Vihara,Bodiand Dewala or within those premises.\n\n5.Within the camp area specified in above section 2,selling and distribution of all food to pilgrims and selling of othercommodities and allowed in the 24 permanent building or the Officer in-charge of the camp. The area beyond 20ft,from the drainage system of both sides of Palle Veediya,Mada Veediya.Dutugamunu Vishrama Shala Mawatha\n\nI fldgi : f\u00feoh - Y%S ,xld m%cd;dka;%sl iudcjd\u00a7 ckrcfha w;s \u00fafYI .ei\u00dc m;%h - 2019'08'13PART I : SECTION I - GAZETTE EXTRAORDINARY OF THE DEMOCRATIC SOCIALIST REPUBLIC OF SRI LANKA \u2013 13.08.2019\n\n(Pilgrims road) Ammodilla road, Badulla Mahiyangana main road, Bodimaluwa Mawatha and the road in front ofthe \u201cSangawasa\u201d(Bikku abode),prescribed as the way of perehara procession by the \u201cBasnayaka Nilame\u201d, is re-served for business purposes.\n\n6.Near by Sangamiththaramara from the clock tower in Badulla main road to sids of the road and front of thepermanent shop it is trading activities by me.\n\n7.Establishing tempory stalls/ mobile stalls and selling goods is entirely prohibited in the camp Including the areaof road sides along the Mahaweli river (comprised to temple land) except as permitted in statement 04 & 05mentioned .\n\n8.Parking of private vehicles in the main street is hereby prohibited and no person shall enter any type of vehiclein to the camp area including bicycles and bullock carts without a permit issues by me or the officer in charge ofthe camp."
